{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "Footnote 3 is supplied and attaches to both XML and PDF methods. The extraction's missing-footnote and unresolved-antecedent statements are stale. The web-form method has no marker 3; extending this certificate requirement to it is unsupported.",
    "PDF upload is a permitted method subject to the prescribed format and e-Cert requirement. The extracted permission is supported as a method choice, not as unconditional authorization or proof of complete compliance.",
    "The date-only candidate includes the period before 9:00am on 2 February 2026; the operational-launch candidates exclude it. The source states both a date-effective channel rule and a 9:00am operational launch. Preserve these competing interpretations of 'following its implementation'; they are not executable equivalents.",
    "The governing timezone is not explicit in the source. An authoritative timezone basis is missing for instant-based classification, with no identifiable supplied dependency ID. Inclusion of the exact launch instant also requires an interpretation of 'following its implementation'.",
    "The blackout provision authorizes direct contact for urgent submissions; it does not establish that every contact constitutes an actual STR submission. Do not infer unrestricted alternative-channel permission or apply the post-launch rule throughout the blackout.",
    "node.29b224046d115582fbf223fb returns FALSE for a known non-submission within licensed-firm scope; the other event candidates return OUT_OF_SCOPE. This distinction needs a consistent assessment-domain interpretation.",
    "The historical questions do not assess whether a duty remains outstanding. A later STREAMS 2 resubmission does not erase the original triggering event. FALSE does not certify submission compliance.",
    "The history candidate delegates event existence and sufficient negative-history evidence to a supplied aggregate. Its formula does not verify either property.",
    "The original-submitter scope in node.8caddb7a4c29338c1d340db1 and the responsible-entity scope in node.fc565a946804e1633024b4d3 may differ for agents or third-party filings. The circular does not expressly resolve that attribution; do not silently exclude reports submitted on a licensed firm's behalf.",
    "The prescribed PDF specification and separately provided XML schema are missing. All supplied external dependency hashes are null, and their IDs have no descriptive mappings; no AVAILABLE assessment or catalogue assignment is justified.",
    "JFIU's promised resubmission guidance is not supplied. It may clarify procedure or disputed boundaries, but the circular does not make issuance of that guidance a precondition to the stated duty."
  ],
